-- Companies Act 1967 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition: s 171 -- the secretary of a company.
-- Layer 1 (the law, objectively). Part sgb2. Every top-level name begins with the label of its provision.
--
-- HOW IT READS. Every company must have one or more secretaries, each a natural person living in Singapore and not debarred under s 155B (a). The directors must take all reasonable steps to see that each secretary
-- appears to them to have the requisite knowledge and experience (1A); in a public company each secretary must meet (1AA). A person appointed secretary must file a declaration of consent at the time of the appointment
-- (1B). A sole director must not act as secretary (1E). The office must not be left vacant for more than 6 months (4A). What the Act says of "debarred" (s 155B), of "public company", "private company" and "registered
-- qualified individual" is a fact here. The Act's own prescribed requirements (1AA)(b) and the prescribed form (1B) are inputs.

§ `Section 171(1): the secretaries every company must have`

DECLARE `s 171 act` IS ONE OF
    `s 171(1) have one or more secretaries each of whom is a natural person resident in Singapore and not debarred`
    `s 171(1A) take all reasonable steps to secure that each secretary appears to the directors to have the requisite knowledge and experience`
    `s 171(1AA) take all reasonable steps to secure that each secretary of the public company satisfies subsection (1AA)(a) or (b)`
    `s 171(1B) file with the Registrar a declaration that the person consents to act as secretary`
    `s 171(1E) act or be appointed as the secretary of the company`
    `s 171(3) be present at the registered office on the days and at the hours it is to be accessible to the public`
    `s 171(4A) fill the vacancy in the office of secretary`

-- (1): "each of whom must be a natural person who has his or her principal or only place of residence in Singapore and who is not debarred under section 155B from acting as secretary".
-- src:14556 | 171.—(1) Every company must have one or more secretaries each
-- src:14557 | of whom must be a natural person who has his or her principal or only
-- src:14558 | place of residence in Singapore and who is not debarred under
-- src:14559 | section 155B from acting as secretary of the company.
@ref s 171(1) (src:14556-14559)
GIVEN `the person is a natural person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has his or her principal or only place of residence in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is debarred under section 155B from acting as secretary of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 171(1) the person is qualified to be a secretary of the company` MEANS
    IF `the person is a natural person` AND `the person has his or her principal or only place of residence in Singapore` AND (NOT `the person is debarred under section 155B from acting as secretary of the company`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "each of whom must be a natural person who has his or her principal or only place of residence in Singapore and who is not debarred under section 155B" (a bare "must" not done: the provision's own question, fork F-171-1 in NOTES.md)

-- src:14556 | 171.—(1) Every company must have one or more secretaries each
-- src:14557 | of whom must be a natural person who has his or her principal or only
-- src:14558 | place of residence in Singapore and who is not debarred under
-- src:14559 | section 155B from acting as secretary of the company.
@ref s 171(1) (src:14556-14559)
GIVEN `the number of secretaries the company has` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 171(1) the company has one or more secretaries` MEANS
    IF `the number of secretaries the company has` AT LEAST 1
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Every company must have one or more secretaries" (a bare "must" not done: the provision's own question, fork F-171-1 in NOTES.md)

-- No period: "Every company must have one or more secretaries" has no time for the company to appoint one, so the rule can never reach BREACH ("Rules with no breach path" in NOTES.md).
-- src:14556 | 171.—(1) Every company must have one or more secretaries each
-- src:14557 | of whom must be a natural person who has his or her principal or only
-- src:14558 | place of residence in Singapore and who is not debarred under
-- src:14559 | section 155B from acting as secretary of the company.
@ref s 171(1) (src:14556-14559)
GIVEN `the name of the company` IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 171 act`
`s 171(1) the company must have one or more secretaries each of whom is qualified` MEANS
    PARTY Company `the name of the company`
    MUST `s 171(1) have one or more secretaries each of whom is a natural person resident in Singapore and not debarred`
    HENCE FULFILLED

§ `Section 171(1A), (1AA), (1AB): the duties of the directors, and the Registrar's power`

