GIVEN `each secretary of the company appears to the directors to have the requisite knowledge and experience to discharge the functions of secretary of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 171(1A) the directors have secured that each secretary appears to them to have the requisite knowledge and experience` MEANS
    IF `each secretary of the company appears to the directors to have the requisite knowledge and experience to discharge the functions of secretary of the company`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "It is the duty of the directors of a company to take all reasonable steps to secure that each secretary of the company is a person who appears to them to have the requisite knowledge and experience" (a bare "must" not done: the provision's own question, fork F-171-1)

-- (1A) and (1AA): "all reasonable steps", with no period: no breach path.
-- src:14563 | (1A) It is the duty of the directors of a company to take all
