-- src:14568 | (1AA) In addition, it is the duty of the directors of a public company
-- src:14569 | to take all reasonable steps to secure that each secretary of the
-- src:14570 | company is a person who —
-- src:14575 | (a) on 15 May 1987 held the office of secretary in that
-- src:14576 | company and continued to hold that office on 15 May
-- src:14577 | 2003; or
-- src:14579 | (b) satisfies such requirements relating to experience,
-- src:14580 | professional and academic requirements and membership
-- src:14581 | of professional associations, as may be prescribed.
@ref s 171(1AA) (src:14568-14581)
GIVEN `the company is a public company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the secretary on 15 May 1987 held the office of secretary in the company and continued to hold that office on 15 May 2003` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the secretary satisfies the requirements prescribed relating to experience, professional and academic requirements and membership of professional associations` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 171(1AA) the secretary of the public company is a person the directors must take all reasonable steps to secure` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the company is a public company`)
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the duty of the directors of a public company" limits the duty to public companies, with no "only"; the subsection says nothing of another company
    ELSE IF `the secretary on 15 May 1987 held the office of secretary in the company and continued to hold that office on 15 May 2003` OR `the secretary satisfies the requirements prescribed relating to experience, professional and academic requirements and membership of professional associations`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "each secretary of the company is a person who (a) on 15 May 1987 held the office of secretary in that company and continued to hold that office on 15 May 2003; or (b) satisfies such requirements ... as may be prescribed" (a closed pair of alternatives; a bare "must" not done: fork F-171-1)

