§ `Section 171(1B), (1C), (1D): the declaration, the old secretary, and the word secretary`

-- (1B): "must, at the time of his or her appointment, by himself or herself or through a registered qualified individual authorised by him or her, file with the Registrar a declaration in the prescribed form that he or she
-- consents to act as secretary and providing the prescribed particulars". "At the time of" is read as: not later than the day of the appointment (fork F-171-1B).
-- src:14593 | (1B) Any person who is appointed by the directors of a company as
-- src:14594 | a secretary must, at the time of his or her appointment, by himself or
-- src:14595 | herself or through a registered qualified individual authorised by him
-- src:14596 | or her, file with the Registrar a declaration in the prescribed form that
-- src:14597 | he or she consents to act as secretary and providing the prescribed
-- src:14598 | particulars.
@ref s 171(1B) (src:14593-14598)
GIVEN `the day the person was appointed as a secretary by the directors` IS A DATE
      `the day the declaration was filed with the Registrar` IS A DATE
      `the declaration is in the prescribed form, states that the person consents to act as secretary and gives the prescribed particulars` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the filing was made by the person or through a registered qualified individual authorised by the person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 171(1B) the person filed the declaration at the time of the appointment` MEANS
    IF    `the declaration is in the prescribed form, states that the person consents to act as secretary and gives the prescribed particulars`
      AND `the filing was made by the person or through a registered qualified individual authorised by the person`
      AND `period: the date is not later than the end of a period after` `the day the person was appointed as a secretary by the directors` `the day the declaration was filed with the Registrar` 0 Days
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must, at the time of his or her appointment, by himself or herself or through a registered qualified individual authorised by him or her, file with the Registrar a declaration in the prescribed form" (a period the text fixes in its own words: the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (a))

-- src:14593 | (1B) Any person who is appointed by the directors of a company as
-- src:14594 | a secretary must, at the time of his or her appointment, by himself or
-- src:14595 | herself or through a registered qualified individual authorised by him
-- src:14596 | or her, file with the Registrar a declaration in the prescribed form that
-- src:14597 | he or she consents to act as secretary and providing the prescribed
-- src:14598 | particulars.
@ref s 171(1B) (src:14593-14598)
GIVEN `the name of the person` IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 171 act`
`s 171(1B) the person appointed as a secretary must file the declaration with the Registrar at the time of the appointment` MEANS
    PARTY Individual `the name of the person`
    MUST `s 171(1B) file with the Registrar a declaration that the person consents to act as secretary`
    WITHIN 0
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Individual `the name of the person` BECAUSE "the person appointed as a secretary did not file with the Registrar, at the time of the appointment, a declaration that he or she consents to act as secretary"

-- (1C): "A person to whom subsection (1AA)(a) applies who, after 15 May 1987, becomes a secretary of another company and is not qualified to act as secretary under subsection (1AA)(b) is not to be regarded as
-- being a person who is qualified to discharge the functions of secretary under this subsection".
-- src:14602 | (1C) A person to whom subsection (1AA)(a) applies who, after
-- src:14603 | 15 May 1987, becomes a secretary of another company and is not
-- src:14604 | qualified to act as secretary under subsection (1AA)(b) is not to be
-- src:14605 | regarded as being a person who is qualified to discharge the functions
-- src:14606 | of secretary under this subsection.
@ref s 171(1C) (src:14602-14606)
GIVEN `subsection (1AA)(a) applies to the person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the person became a secretary of another company` IS A DATE
      `the person is qualified to act as secretary under subsection (1AA)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 171(1C) the person is not to be regarded as qualified to discharge the functions of secretary under subsection (1A)` MEANS
    IF    `subsection (1AA)(a) applies to the person`
      AND `the day the person became a secretary of another company` GREATER THAN Date 15 5 1987
      AND (NOT `the person is qualified to act as secretary under subsection (1AA)(b)`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A person to whom subsection (1AA)(a) applies who, after 15 May 1987, becomes a secretary of another company and is not qualified" is not to be regarded as qualified; the subsection says nothing of any other person

-- src:14610 | (1D) In this section and sections 173 to 173I, “secretary” includes
-- src:14611 | an assistant or deputy secretary.
@ref s 171(1D) (src:14610-14611)
GIVEN `the person is a secretary` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is an assistant or deputy secretary` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 171(1D) the person is within the word secretary in the section and in sections 173 to 173I` MEANS
    IF `the person is a secretary` OR `the person is an assistant or deputy secretary`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "“secretary” includes an assistant or deputy secretary" does not say that no other person is a secretary

§ `Section 171(1E): a sole director is not to act as secretary`

-- (1E): "Where a director is the sole director of a company, he or she must not act or be appointed as the secretary of the company".
-- src:14615 | (1E) Where a director is the sole director of a company, he or she
-- src:14616 | must not act or be appointed as the secretary of the company.
@ref s 171(1E) (src:14615-14616)
GIVEN `the person is the sole director of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 171(1E) the person must not act or be appointed as the secretary of the company` MEANS
    IF `the person is the sole director of the company`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where a director is the sole director of a company, he or she must not act or be appointed as the secretary" bars the sole director only by its own wording and says nothing of another person (the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (c))

-- src:14615 | (1E) Where a director is the sole director of a company, he or she
-- src:14616 | must not act or be appointed as the secretary of the company.
@ref s 171(1E) (src:14615-14616)
GIVEN `the name of the director` IS A STRING
      `the person is the sole director of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 171 act`
`s 171(1E) the sole director must not act or be appointed as the secretary of the company` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the person is the sole director of the company`)
    THEN FULFILLED
    ELSE PARTY Director `the name of the director`
         SHANT `s 171(1E) act or be appointed as the secretary of the company`
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY Director `the name of the director` BECAUSE "the sole director of the company acted or was appointed as the secretary of the company"

§ `Section 171(2) and (3): the secretaries are appointed by the directors, and one is present at the registered office`

-- (2): "Subsection (1) does not operate to prevent a corporation which was acting as the secretary of a company immediately before 29 December 1967 from continuing to act as secretary of that company for a period
-- of 12 months after that date." The 12 months ended on 29 December 1968; the row is inert, reason 2 (a transitional provision that affects no one now).

