    ELSE IF `a secretary or his or her agent or clerk of the private company is readily contactable by a person at the registered office by telephone or other means of instantaneous communication during those times`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "need not be physically present ... if a secretary or his or her agent or clerk of the private company is readily contactable" (a failed "if": marginal reading (a))

