§ `Section 171(4), (4A) and (5): the vacancy, and director and secretary in one person`

DECLARE `s 171(4) kind of person` IS ONE OF
    `s 171(4) an assistant or deputy secretary`
    `s 171(4) an officer of the company authorised generally or specially in that behalf by the directors`
    `s 171(4) another person`

-- (4): "anything required or authorised to be done by or in relation to the secretary may, if the office is vacant or for any other reason the secretary is not capable of acting, be done by or in relation to any
-- assistant or deputy secretary or, if there is no assistant or deputy secretary capable of acting, by or in relation to any officer of the company authorised generally or specially in that behalf by the directors."
-- src:14641 | (4) Subject to subsection (4A), anything required or authorised to
-- src:14642 | be done by or in relation to the secretary may, if the office is vacant or
-- src:14643 | for any other reason the secretary is not capable of acting, be done by
-- src:14644 | or in relation to any assistant or deputy secretary or, if there is no
-- src:14645 | assistant or deputy secretary capable of acting, by or in relation to any
-- src:14646 | officer of the company authorised generally or specially in that behalf
-- src:14647 | by the directors.
@ref s 171(4) (src:14641-14647)
GIVEN kind IS A `s 171(4) kind of person`
      `the office of secretary is vacant or for any other reason the secretary is not capable of acting` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is no assistant or deputy secretary capable of acting` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the directors have authorised the officer generally or specially in that behalf` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 171(4) the thing may be done by or in relation to the person in place of the secretary` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `s 171(4) another person` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection names an assistant or deputy secretary and an authorised officer, and says nothing of any other person
    WHEN `s 171(4) an assistant or deputy secretary`
         THEN (IF `the office of secretary is vacant or for any other reason the secretary is not capable of acting` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING)   -- NOTHING-kind (grant): a function named for a permission ("may ... be done") whose "if" gate failed answers NOTHING, with a fork line: limit 1 of the ruling of 2026-11-12 (fork F-171-4)
    OTHERWISE
         (IF    `the office of secretary is vacant or for any other reason the secretary is not capable of acting`
            AND `there is no assistant or deputy secretary capable of acting`
            AND `the directors have authorised the officer generally or specially in that behalf`
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE NOTHING)   -- NOTHING-kind (grant): the same, for the authorised officer (fork F-171-4)

-- (4A): "The office of secretary must not be left vacant for more than 6 months at any one time." The text names no bearer; the company, whose office it is, is taken as the bearer (fork F-171-4A).
-- src:14649 | (4A) The office of secretary must not be left vacant for more than
-- src:14650 | 6 months at any one time.
@ref s 171(4A) (src:14649-14650)
GIVEN `the day the office of secretary became vacant` IS A DATE
      `the day the vacancy was filled` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 171(4A) the office of secretary was not left vacant for more than 6 months` MEANS
    IF `period: the date is not later than the end of a period after` `the day the office of secretary became vacant` `the day the vacancy was filled` 6 Months
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The office of secretary must not be left vacant for more than 6 months at any one time" (a flat negative; a period the text fixes in its own words: the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (a))

-- src:14649 | (4A) The office of secretary must not be left vacant for more than
-- src:14650 | 6 months at any one time.
@ref s 171(4A) (src:14649-14650)
GIVEN `the day the office of secretary became vacant` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 171(4A) the number of days from the day the office became vacant to the last day of the 6 months` MEANS
    (`period: the last day of a period after` `the day the office of secretary became vacant` 6 Months) MINUS `the day the office of secretary became vacant`

-- src:14649 | (4A) The office of secretary must not be left vacant for more than
-- src:14650 | 6 months at any one time.
@ref s 171(4A) (src:14649-14650)
GIVEN `the name of the company` IS A STRING
      `the number of days from the day the office became vacant to the last day of the 6 months` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 171 act`
`s 171(4A) the company must not leave the office of secretary vacant for more than 6 months` MEANS
    PARTY Company `the name of the company`
    MUST `s 171(4A) fill the vacancy in the office of secretary`
    WITHIN `the number of days from the day the office became vacant to the last day of the 6 months`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Company `the name of the company` BECAUSE "the company left the office of secretary vacant for more than 6 months"

-- src:14652 | (5) A provision requiring or authorising a thing to be done by or in
-- src:14653 | relation to a director and the secretary is not satisfied by its being
-- src:14654 | done by or in relation to the same person acting both as director and
-- src:14655 | as, or in place of, the secretary.
@ref s 171(5) (src:14652-14655)
GIVEN `the thing was done by or in relation to the same person acting both as director and as, or in place of, the secretary` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 171(5) the thing done satisfies a provision requiring it to be done by or in relation to a director and the secretary` MEANS
    IF `the thing was done by or in relation to the same person acting both as director and as, or in place of, the secretary`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A provision requiring or authorising a thing to be done by or in relation to a director and the secretary is not satisfied by its being done by or in relation to the same person acting both as director and as, or in place of, the secretary" (a flat negative: N2 of 2026-11-04)
    ELSE NOTHING      -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection says when the provision is not satisfied and says nothing of a thing done by two persons
